# Security and cache headers for Static Assets (security §14, D12.8).
#
# The CSP here carries ONLY the directives a <meta> tag cannot express: frame-ancestors is
# ignored in meta, and base-uri / form-action belong with it. Everything about scripts, styles,
# images and fonts is emitted by Astro as a meta CSP with per-file SHA-256 hashes
# (astro.config.ts, experimental.csp). The two policies are enforced independently, so no
# directive may appear in both — a header "style-src 'self'" would intersect with the meta
# policy and block the inlined stylesheet.
#
# HOW RULES COMBINE — read this before adding one. Every rule that matches a request applies, in
# file order, and a header set by two of them is JOINED with a comma, not replaced (Cloudflare
# docs, "Custom headers"). Measured on 12/11/2026 under `wrangler dev`, before this file was ever
# deployed: as first written, it served the fonts with
# "public, max-age=300, public, max-age=31536000, immutable" — two max-age values, which a cache
# is entitled to treat as stale — and the kill switch with "public, max-age=300, no-cache".
# A specific rule must first DETACH what "/*" set ("! Header-Name"), then set its own value.
# "/*" stays first; scripts/headers.test.ts holds both points.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

# The preview host (D15.12) is where the app is built before launch: never indexed. An absolute
# URL scopes the rule to that hostname, so the apex is untouched.
https://beta.cestecritla.fr/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Content-addressed by the build: safe to freeze for a year.
/_astro/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/fonts/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The search index and its titles carry the corpus version in their name (D15.7): a new state of
# the book gets new files, so these can be frozen too.
/data/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Share previews are versioned by corpus_version in their path (D13.2), so a re-crawl changes
# the URL rather than the bytes: a permanent link never breaks and caches renew on their own.
/og/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The only client-side kill switch (D12.8). Revalidated on every start, BEFORE effectiveDate().
# Never immutable, never stale-while-revalidate: those would make the L49 freeze unreachable.
/flags.json
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8

# The service worker is the only component able to make an outage permanent (H-PLA-8).
/sw.js
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/sw-kill.js
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# The beacon is the only server route in v1/v2. The Worker sets these itself (this file is not
# applied to a Worker's own responses); repeated here so an asset can never be served under
# /api/ with a cacheable or referrer-leaking policy.
/api/*
  ! Cache-Control
  ! Referrer-Policy
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
